          "disposition": "superseded_by_grid_cleanup",
          "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept.\nAsset type: original Mosslume basic-tool inventory icon atlas, truly transparent PNG, four equal columns by two equal rows.\nPrimary request: exactly SEVEN different practical handcrafted tools, one per cell, last bottom-right cell empty and transparent. Reading order: top row wood-handled axe, wood-handled pickaxe, shovel, hoe; bottom row copper-and-teal watering can, simple wooden fishing rod with a small reel and line, carpenter's hammer, EMPTY.\nStyle: crisp carefully authored low-resolution pixel-art inventory icons, each designed to remain readable at logical 32x32, enlarged for viewing. Strong clean dark outline, deliberate square pixel clusters, matte iron/copper and warm brown wood handles, restrained teal accents to match the cozy forest-island game Mosslume. Same consistent three-quarter item view and light source in each cell, clear shapes, modest highlights, original designs. Not clipart, not realistic photographs, not smooth 3D, not painted on cards.\nComposition: clean wide 2:1 atlas with eight equal invisible square cells, icon centered with consistent padding and optical scale in each occupied cell, no parts crossing a cell boundary. Axe head has one blade, pickaxe has pointed curved ends, hoe has one right-angled flat blade distinct from shovel and pickaxe. All seven objects must be visibly distinct. Transparent background and gutters. No character, hands, labels, text, numbers, borders, slot frames, grid lines, scenery, shadows or watermark."
        },
